module CantonStake.Setup where

-- Party allocation is handled manually via Canton Console for LocalNet/DevNet.
--
-- After parties are allocated, bootstrap the default 75/25 BeneficiarySplit
-- via the JSON Ledger API or Canton Console:
--
--   1. As `appProvider` (the operator), create a BeneficiarySplit with
--      label="default", weights=[(appProvider, 0.25), (delegator, 0.75)],
--      version=0, updatedAt=<ISO timestamp>.
--   2. Capture the resulting contractId from the create event.
--   3. Set BENEFICIARY_SPLIT_CID=<cid> in the backend .env so the
--      orchestrator can pass it to StakingPosition_RecordStake.
--
-- Verified recipe (JSON Ledger API v2, Canton 3.5 / cn-quickstart LocalNet,
-- exercised 2026-08-14). Two encoding details that the old pseudocode got
-- wrong and that both return HTTP 500 "Expected ujson.Str":
--   * `[(Party, Decimal)]` tuples encode as records with `_1` / `_2` keys,
--     NOT as two-element JSON arrays.
--   * Daml `Int` encodes as a JSON *string* ("0"), not a JSON number (0).
--     The same rule applies to EvmProof.blockNumber and to
--     StakingPosition_ConfirmUnbond's unbondingReadyEpoch.
--
--   POST http://localhost:3975/v2/commands/submit-and-wait-for-transaction
--   Authorization: Bearer <CANTON_AUTH_TOKEN>
--   { "commands": {
--       "commands": [{ "CreateCommand": {
--         "templateId": "#cantonstake:CantonStake.Staking:BeneficiarySplit",
--         "createArguments": {
--           "operator": "<appProvider>",
--           "label": "default",
--           "weights": [ { "_1": "<appProvider>", "_2": "0.25" },
--                        { "_1": "<delegator>",   "_2": "0.75" } ],
--           "version": "0",
--           "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T00:00:00Z"
--         }}}],
--       "commandId": "setup-split-1", "actAs": ["<appProvider>"],
--       "readAs": [], "workflowId": "cantonstake-setup",
--       "deduplicationPeriod": { "Empty": {} }, "disclosedContracts": [],
--       "synchronizerId": "", "packageIdSelectionPreference": [] } }
--
-- Prerequisite: upload the DAR to each participant that hosts a stakeholder
-- party (app-provider :3975 and app-user :2975 on LocalNet):
--   curl -X POST http://localhost:3975/v2/packages \
--        -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
--        -H "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" \
--        --data-binary @.daml/dist/cantonstake-0.0.1.dar
--
-- The default weights match the inline 75/25 split that the legacy
-- USE_LEGACY_MARKERS=true path emits, so attribution is consistent across
-- both paths during the CIP-0104 rollout.
